### 3. BERT & Hybrid "Sayqallash" Engine
Introduce a local BERT model (specifically `uzbert` or a multilingual variant) for contextual word masking and grammatical analysis.

#### [NEW] [bert_engine.py](file:///c:/Users/Администратор/Desktop/2/backend/bert_engine.py)
*   Initialize `transformers` pipeline using `mohir/uzbert-v1` or a similar high-quality Uzbek model.
*   Implement background thread for model initialization.
*   Integrate into `/sayqallash` and `/suggest-edits`.

### 2. Tahrirchi.db Integration (8.7M words)
Integrate the 8.7M word `tahrirchi.db` (located at `backend/tahrirchi.db`) and implement parallel import/optimization scripts.

#### [MODIFY] [db.py](file:///c:/Users/Администратор/Desktop/2/backend/db.py)
*   Connect to `tahrirchi.db`.
*   Implement `search_dictionary(word, lang)` using the `dictionary` table (8.7M words).
*   Use `normalize_for_lookup` from `transliterate.py` for cross-alphabet search.
*   Sync `sayqallash_rules` with `tahrirchi.db`'s `corrections` and `confirmed_words`.

#### [MODIFY] [main.py](file:///c:/Users/Администратор/Desktop/2/backend/main.py)
*   Update `/sayqallash` and `/suggest-edits` to use a **Hybrid Approach**: Check BERT/Local DB first → Fallback to Claude for complex linguistic nuances.

